Below is a compact “road‑map” showing  

• Which columns in the `bigquery-public-data.usda_nass_agriculture.crops` table are useful for the request,  
• Ten step‑by‑step SELECT statements (each limited to 20 rows) that go from simple exploration to the final query that returns every state’s 2022 corn‑and‑mushroom production totals side‑by‑side.  

Relevant columns and how they are used  
• `year` – filter on 2022  
• `group_desc` – distinguishes FIELD CROPS vs HORTICULTURE  
• `commodity_desc` – distinguishes CORN vs MUSHROOMS  
• `statisticcat_desc` – keep only ‘PRODUCTION’ rows  
• `unit_desc` – for corn, make sure it is ‘BU’ (bushels)  
• `agg_level_desc` – keep only ‘STATE’ rows  
• `state_alpha` / `state_name` – state identifiers to display  
• `value` – the production figure we need (already numeric in this table)  

SQL 1 – peek at 2022 “PRODUCTION” rows
```sql
--Description: Grab 20 sample 2022 PRODUCTION rows at the STATE level.
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usda_nass_agriculture.crops`
WHERE year = 2022
  AND statisticcat_desc = 'PRODUCTION'
  AND agg_level_desc = 'STATE'
LIMIT 20;
```

SQL 2 – what commodities exist in FIELD CROPS (2022)?
```sql
--Description: Distinct commodities under FIELD CROPS in 2022.
SELECT DISTINCT commodity_desc
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usda_nass_agriculture.crops`
WHERE year = 2022
  AND group_desc = 'FIELD CROPS'
ORDER BY commodity_desc
LIMIT 20;
```

SQL 3 – confirm corn rows satisfy the unit requirement
```sql
--Description: Check the distinct units used for CORN production in 2022.
SELECT DISTINCT unit_desc
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usda_nass_agriculture.crops`
WHERE year = 2022
  AND commodity_desc = 'CORN'
  AND statisticcat_desc = 'PRODUCTION'
  AND agg_level_desc = 'STATE'
LIMIT 20;
```

SQL 4 – list 2022 corn production by state
```sql
--Description: Corn production (BU) in 2022, per state.
SELECT state_alpha,
       state_name,
       value AS corn_bu
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usda_nass_agriculture.crops`
WHERE year = 2022
  AND group_desc = 'FIELD CROPS'
  AND commodity_desc = 'CORN'
  AND statisticcat_desc = 'PRODUCTION'
  AND agg_level_desc = 'STATE'
  AND unit_desc = 'BU'
  AND value IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

SQL 5 – list 2022 mushroom production by state
```sql
--Description: Mushroom production in 2022, per state (value is already in the proper unit recorded by NASS).
SELECT state_alpha,
       state_name,
       value AS mushrooms_val
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usda_nass_agriculture.crops`
WHERE year = 2022
  AND group_desc = 'HORTICULTURE'
  AND commodity_desc = 'MUSHROOMS'
  AND statisticcat_desc = 'PRODUCTION'
  AND agg_level_desc = 'STATE'
  AND value IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

SQL 6 – UNION the two lists to view them stacked
```sql
--Description: Combine corn & mushroom rows (stacked).
SELECT 'CORN'       AS commodity, state_alpha, state_name, value
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usda_nass_agriculture.crops`
WHERE year = 2022 AND commodity_desc = 'CORN'       AND statisticcat_desc = 'PRODUCTION'
  AND agg_level_desc = 'STATE' AND unit_desc = 'BU' AND value IS NOT NULL

UNION ALL
SELECT 'MUSHROOMS'  AS commodity, state_alpha, state_name, value
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usda_nass_agriculture.crops`
WHERE year = 2022 AND commodity_desc = 'MUSHROOMS'  AND statisticcat_desc = 'PRODUCTION'
  AND agg_level_desc = 'STATE'                       AND value IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

SQL 7 – pivot the UNION with conditional aggregation
```sql
--Description: Pivot the previous union so each state is one row with two columns.
SELECT
  state_alpha,
  state_name,
  SUM(CASE WHEN commodity = 'CORN'      THEN value END) AS corn_bu,
  SUM(CASE WHEN commodity = 'MUSHROOMS' THEN value END) AS mushrooms_val
FROM (
  -- same UNION as in SQL 6
  SELECT 'CORN' AS commodity, state_alpha, state_name, value
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.usda_nass_agriculture.crops`
  WHERE year = 2022 AND commodity_desc = 'CORN'
    AND statisticcat_desc = 'PRODUCTION' AND agg_level_desc = 'STATE'
    AND unit_desc = 'BU' AND value IS NOT NULL

  UNION ALL
  SELECT 'MUSHROOMS', state_alpha, state_name, value
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.usda_nass_agriculture.crops`
  WHERE year = 2022 AND commodity_desc = 'MUSHROOMS'
    AND statisticcat_desc = 'PRODUCTION' AND agg_level_desc = 'STATE'
    AND value IS NOT NULL
)
GROUP BY state_alpha, state_name
ORDER BY state_alpha
LIMIT 20;
```

SQL 8 – same as 7 but using two JOINed sub‑queries
```sql
--Description: Bring corn and mushrooms together via LEFT JOIN on state.
WITH corn AS (
  SELECT state_alpha, state_name, value AS corn_bu
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.usda_nass_agriculture.crops`
  WHERE year = 2022
    AND commodity_desc = 'CORN'
    AND statisticcat_desc = 'PRODUCTION'
    AND agg_level_desc = 'STATE'
    AND unit_desc = 'BU'
    AND value IS NOT NULL
),
mush AS (
  SELECT state_alpha, state_name, value AS mushrooms_val
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.usda_nass_agriculture.crops`
  WHERE year = 2022
    AND commodity_desc = 'MUSHROOMS'
    AND statisticcat_desc = 'PRODUCTION'
    AND agg_level_desc = 'STATE'
    AND value IS NOT NULL
)
SELECT
  c.state_alpha,
  c.state_name,
  c.corn_bu,
  m.mushrooms_val
FROM corn AS c
LEFT JOIN mush AS m
USING (state_alpha, state_name)
ORDER BY state_alpha
LIMIT 20;
```

SQL 9 – add total U.S. row (roll‑up)
```sql
--Description: Same join, but append a U.S. total row with GROUPING SETS.
WITH corn AS (
  SELECT state_alpha, state_name, value AS corn_bu
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.usda_nass_agriculture.crops`
  WHERE year = 2022
    AND commodity_desc = 'CORN'
    AND statisticcat_desc = 'PRODUCTION'
    AND agg_level_desc = 'STATE'
    AND unit_desc = 'BU'
    AND value IS NOT NULL
),
mush AS (
  SELECT state_alpha, state_name, value AS mushrooms_val
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.usda_nass_agriculture.crops`
  WHERE year = 2022
    AND commodity_desc = 'MUSHROOMS'
    AND statisticcat_desc = 'PRODUCTION'
    AND agg_level_desc = 'STATE'
    AND value IS NOT NULL
)
SELECT
  state_alpha,
  state_name,
  SUM(corn_bu)        AS corn_bu,
  SUM(mushrooms_val)  AS mushrooms_val
FROM (
  SELECT state_alpha, state_name, corn_bu, NULL AS mushrooms_val FROM corn
  UNION ALL
  SELECT state_alpha, state_name, NULL,  mushrooms_val FROM mush
)
GROUP BY GROUPING SETS ( (state_alpha, state_name), () )
ORDER BY state_alpha
LIMIT 20;
```

SQL 10 – FINAL answer query (all states, both commodities)
```sql
--Description: Final query – 2022 corn (bushels) and mushroom production per state.
WITH corn AS (
  SELECT
    state_alpha,
    state_name,
    value AS corn_bu
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.usda_nass_agriculture.crops`
  WHERE year = 2022
    AND group_desc = 'FIELD CROPS'
    AND commodity_desc = 'CORN'
    AND statisticcat_desc = 'PRODUCTION'
    AND agg_level_desc = 'STATE'
    AND unit_desc = 'BU'
    AND value IS NOT NULL
),
mush AS (
  SELECT
    state_alpha,
    state_name,
    value AS mushrooms_val
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.usda_nass_agriculture.crops`
  WHERE year = 2022
    AND group_desc = 'HORTICULTURE'
    AND commodity_desc = 'MUSHROOMS'
    AND statisticcat_desc = 'PRODUCTION'
    AND agg_level_desc = 'STATE'
    AND value IS NOT NULL
)
SELECT
  c.state_alpha           AS state,
  c.state_name,
  c.corn_bu,
  COALESCE(m.mushrooms_val, 0) AS mushrooms
FROM corn AS c
LEFT JOIN mush  AS m
USING (state_alpha, state_name)
ORDER BY state_alpha;
```

Run SQL 10 (removing the `LIMIT` if you want the complete list) to obtain one row per U.S. state containing:  

• `corn_bu`  – 2022 corn production in bushels,  
• `mushrooms` – 2022 mushroom production figure (0 if none reported for that state).
